7\nVersion: 3.11\n\n--- Record 444 ---\nComponent: UI Theme Designer\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Theming Base Content for CF and Neo.\nDescription: The base theming content is updated to version 11.31.1. Review the changes at https://github.com/SAP/theming-base-content/releases.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2025-07-17\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 445 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: API Gateway module: Update to version 2.1.3\nDescription: With this release, we've fixed zero downtime migration progressing in cases where an error occurs during the process.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-16\nValid as Of: 2025-07-16\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 446 ---\nComponent: SAP Task Center\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Intelligent Recommendation - URL Updated\nDescription: The URL for the Intelligent Recommendations destination has been updated. If you have already configured this destination, update the URL property to match the new pattern.   For more information, see Configure the Intelligent Recommendations Destination.\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-15\nValid as Of: 2025-07-15\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 447 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Change in provisioning job behavior\nDescription: Provisioning jobs that skip create and delete operations and only update entities will no longer fail if those entities - previously provisioned from the source to the target system, are deleted in the target. By design, Identity Provisioning runs update jobs only for entities that exist in the target system.  Instead of marking these entities as failed, Identity Provisioning now classifies them as skipped. Therefore, the job status is Successful rather than Finished with Error.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-15\nValid as Of: 2025-07-15\nVersion: 28063\n\n--- Record 448 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Change in provisioning job behavior (Effective July 15, 2025)\nDescription: As of July 15, 2025, provisioning jobs that skip create and delete operations and only update entities will no longer fail if those entities - previously provisioned from the source to the target system - are deleted in the target. By design, Identity Provisioning runs update jobs only for entities that exist in the target system.  Instead of marking these entities as failed, Identity Provisioning will now classify them as skipped. Therefore, the job status will be Successful rather than Finished with Error.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-04\nValid as Of: 2025-07-15\nVersion: 27915\n\n--- Record 449 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Regional Availability\nDescription: Cloud Identity Services is available with a new data center for the Google Cloud infrastructure in Israel. The data center is located in Tel Aviv.  Action: You must add the following IPs to your allowed IP list:  LB IPs - 34.165.59.107, 34.165.82.240    NAT IPs - 34.165.48.136/32, 34.165.90.82/32, 34.165.0.183/32     See Regional Availability.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-15\nValid as Of: 2025-07-15\nVersion: 28063\n\n--- Record 450 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle", "32, 34.165.90.82/32, 34.165.0.183/32     See Regional Availability.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-15\nValid as Of: 2025-07-15\nVersion: 28063\n\n--- Record 450 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Regular Upgrade\nDescription: Cloud Identity Services have been upgraded.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-15\nValid as Of: 2025-07-15\nVersion: 28063\n\n", "--- Record 1061 ---\nComponent: Data Space Integration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Operator \"Exists\" for Company Policies\nDescription: When you create rules for company policies, you can now use the operator exists in combination with the attribute contract reference. Create a new rule, select the attribute contract reference, then select exists. The value of the rule is left empty on purpose to define that the company policy should check if any contract reference exists in the provider's offer.  See Create and Edit Company Policies.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-04-10\nValid as Of: 2025-04-10\nVersion: 2502\n\n--- Record 1062 ---\nComponent: Data Space Integration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Software Version Update\nDescription: The following are the latest versions in Data Space Integration:      Data Space Integration: 1.7.*      Increment: 2502      Tractus-X Eclipse Dataspace Connector: 0.7.6      FOSS Eclipse Dataspace Components: 0.7.2      See also the Release Notes of Catena-X. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-04-10\nValid as Of: 2025-04-10\nVersion: 2502\n\n--- Record 1063 ---\nComponent: Mobile Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Access: BTP Cockpit & Dev Space Manager\nDescription: (Version 2503) To simplify navigation to your SAP BTP Cockpit and Dev Space Manager, we have added direct links in the Mobile Services cockpit.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-04-10\nValid as Of: 2025-04-10\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1064 ---\nComponent: Mobile Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Full Initial Download from Offline Service\nDescription: (Version 2503) We've introduced a new feature labeled as Trigger Initial Download, this feature lets you initiate the full download of app data from the offline service and cancel the full initial download if needed. You can trigger this download from application level also registration level.For more information, see Managing App Users and Device Registrations and Defining Offline Settings for Applications.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-04-10\nValid as Of: 2025-04-10\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1065 ---\nComponent: Mobile Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Include Predefined Annotations\nDescription: (Version 2503) We've introduced a new checkbox to enable predefined annotations for sample OData for testing.  For more information, see Using the Sample ODATA ESPM\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-04-10\nValid as Of: 2025-04-10\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1066 ---\nComponent: Mobile Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Update: Logout Service\nDescription: (Version 2503) When the Logout API is called, it removes registrations for registered users and devices related with the push feature from the server.  For more information, see DELETE User Logout Request and POST User Logout Request.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-04-10\nValid as Of: 2025-04-10\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1067 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: API Gateway module: Update to version 2.11.3\nDescription: We have implemented a watch mechanism to ensure that DNSEntry is up to date with the IP and host of the istio-ingressgateway service. Additionally, we've decreased the default reconciliation time to safeguard against possible scheduling errors.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-04-09\nValid as Of: 2025-04-09\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1068 ---\nComponent: SAP Task Center\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Feedback Option for Documentation\nDescription: You can now provide feedback on the SAP Task Center documentation using the Feedback  Comments function on the SAP Help Portal, without the need to use GitHub. You just need to log in to the SAP Help Portal with your email.   For more information, see Creating Better Documentation Together: SAP Help Portal’s new approach to Collaboration and Feedback.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-04-09\nValid as Of: 2025-04-09\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1069 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Identity Authentication (using SCIM API version 2) - changed behavior\nDescription: Similar to the Local Identity Directory, you can now use Identity Authentication (SCIM API version 2) for reading and writing application-specific groups. Depending on the configured pair of provisioning systems, to ensure successful provisioning, you might need to manually define value mappings for the attribute applicationId in the source or the target system transformations.  For more information, see:    Identity Authentication (Source)  Identity Authentication (Target)  List of Properties→ips.application.id  \nAction: Info only", "\nDescription: Similar to the Local Identity Directory, you can now use Identity Authentication (SCIM API version 2) for reading and writing application-specific groups. Depending on the configured pair of 