res  (Log on with your SAP ID to access this document.)\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-20\nValid as Of: 2024-03-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3263 ---\nComponent: SAP S/⁠4HANA Cloud for Credit Integration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Integration with new credit agency: Ellisphere\nDescription: The credit agency Ellisphere is now connected to SAP S/⁠4HANA Cloud for credit integration.  More information:  Available Credit Agency Products and Features  Your Tasks for Integrating a New Credit Agency\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-20\nValid as Of: 2024-03-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3264 ---\nComponent: SAP Task Center\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Pushing SAP S/4HANA and SAP S/4HANA Cloud Private Edition Tasks Enabled\nDescription: You can now enable task updates to be pushed from SAP S/4HANA or SAP S/4HANA Cloud Private Edition. For more information, see the Prerequisites section and tc.clientId in Connect SAP S/4HANA and SAP Task Center and Connect SAP S/4HANA Cloud Private Edition and SAP Task Center.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-20\nValid as Of: 2024-03-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3265 ---\nComponent: SAP Alert Notification Service\nEnvironment: Other\nTitle: Mutual TLS Authentication using a user-provided certificate issued by SAP Cloud PKI\nDescription: Information about the authentication mechanism “Mutual TLS Authentication using user-provided certificate issued by SAP Cloud PKI” has been added to the documentation. For more information, see:   Cloud Foundry: Credential Management  Neo: Credential Management\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-19\nValid as Of: 2024-03-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3266 ---\nComponent: SAP Build\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Cookie Settings\nDescription: You can now manage your cookie preferences within the settings of the SAP Build.  See Cookie Settings.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-19\nValid as Of: 2024-03-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3267 ---\nComponent: Graph\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Model Extensions and Custom Entity Modeling is supported\nDescription: Extending and customizing business data graphs with model extensions is now available on the Model Extensions tab in Graph. For more information, see the tutorial: API Composition with Graph: Customizing your Business Data Graphs with Model Extensions.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-18\nValid as Of: 2024-03-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3268 ---\nComponent: Integration Advisor\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: DateTime Conversion\nDescription: You can now add global parameters to a source node in DateTime conversion of your mapping guideline.  See: Date Time Conversion\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-18\nValid as Of: 2024-03-18\nVersion: 2401\n\n--- Record 3269 ---\nComponent: Integration Advisor\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Software Version Update\nDescription:   SAP Integration Advisor: 1.84.*    Increment: 2401    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-18\nValid as Of: 2024-03-18\nVersion: 2401\n\n--- Record 3270 ---\nComponent: Integration Assessment\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Software Version Update\nDescription:     Integration Assessment: 1.25.*      Increment: 2401    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-18\nValid as Of: 2024-03-18\nVersion: ", "2024-03-18\nVersion: 2401\n\n--- Record 3270 ---\nComponent: Integration Assessment\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Software Version Update\nDescription:     Integration Assessment: 1.25.*      Increment: 2401    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-18\nValid as Of: 2024-03-18\nVersion: 2401\n\n", "--- Record 21 ---\nComponent: Application for Data Replication and Administration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Option to Improve Pricing Delta Replication Performance\nDescription: The Connect to SAP Cloud screen now has the option Enable Transmit Data in Compact Mode for pricing remote sources. This breaks referential integrity among tables. It is only recommended for when you perform pricing changes with future validity dates.   See: Administration Guide for SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-19\nValid as Of: 2025-10-22\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 22 ---\nComponent: Application for Data Replication and Administration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Show Dependency Profiling Trace\nDescription: There is a new screen to show the dependency profiling trace in Configuration  Trace.   See: Administration Guide for SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-19\nValid as Of: 2025-10-22\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 23 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Data Center: Microsoft Azure in Australia (Sydney)(cf-ap20)\nDescription: SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing used to be available only in:   AWS Europe (Frankfurt) (cf-eu10)  AWS Europe (Frankfurt) EU Access (cf-eu11)  Azure Europe (Netherlands) (cf-eu20)  AWS U.S. East (Virgina) (cf-us10)  AWS Singapore (cf-ap11)    For new contracts, configuration and pricing services now are also available in Microsoft Azure data center in Australia (Sydney)(cf-ap20).  All configuration and pricing services tenants of a customer must be operated in the same data center. It is not possible to run one tenant on AWS and another on Azure, nor to switch data centers for existing tenants.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-19\nValid as Of: 2025-10-22\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 24 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Pre-Production – Stateless Pricing – Condition Supplements in Price Agreements\nDescription: Condition supplements, such as those related to surcharges or discounts, that are linked to a primary condition, can now be processed alongside the primary conditions in stateless price agreement scenarios. This ensures that all dependent pricing elements are considered during price calculation.  See: API Definition, and Development Guide for SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-19\nValid as Of: 2025-10-22\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 25 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Pre-Production – Stateless Pricing – Dynamic Scale Base Types in Price Agreements\nDescription: Price agreements in stateless pricing now support dynamic scale base types as part of the pricing input. Consuming applications can specify the scale base type at runtime, for example, quantity, value, weight, volume. This allows the correct evaluation of scale conditions based on the input during runtime rather than relying only on predefined customizing.  See: API Definition, and Development Guide for SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-19\nValid as Of: 2025-10-22\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 26 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Pre-Production – Stateless Pricing – Validity-Based Selection of Condition Records in Price Agreements\nDescription: Price agreements in stateless pricing now support processing of multiple condition records with the same condition type but different validity periods. The relevant condition record is automatically selected and applied based on the pricing date, ensuring accurate handling of time-dependent conditions.  See: API Definition, and Development Guide for SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-19\nValid as Of: 2025-10-22\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 27 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Pre-Production – US Tax Calculation via External Engine\nDescription: Tax calculation via an external tax engine is now supported for US taxes.  See: API Definition, Development Guide for SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing , and Administration Guide for SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-19\nValid as Of: 2025-10-22\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 28 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Pre-Production– On-Request Tracing\nDescription: Additionally to the existing trace settings ON and OFF, a new setting ON_REQUEST was introduced to collect traces only for a subset of requests. To determine for which requests the traces will be collected, the header parameter x-cps-trace needs to be set. The relevant trace type must be set as a parameter value: CONDITION_DETERMINATION, CONDITION_CALCULATION, EXTENSION, or TAXES_US.  See: API Definition, Development Guide for SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing , andAdministration Guide for SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\n", " only for a subset of requests. To determine for which requests the traces will be collected, the header parameter x-cps-trace needs to be set. The relevant trace type must be set as a parameter value: CONDITION_DETERMINATION, CONDITION_CALCULATION, EXTENSION, or TAXES_US.  See: API Definition, Development Guide for SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing , andAdministration Guide for SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-19\nValid as Of: 2025-10-22\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 29 ---\nComponent: Variant Configuration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Data Center: Microsoft Azure in Australia (Sydney)(cf-ap20)\nDescription: SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing used to be available only in:   AWS Europe (Frankfurt) (cf-eu10)  AWS Europe (Frankfurt) EU Access (cf-eu11)  Azure Europe (Netherlands) (cf-eu20)  AWS U.S. East (Virgina) (cf-us10)  AWS Singapore (cf-ap11)    For new contracts, configuration and pricing services now are also available in Microsoft Azure data center in Australia (Sydney)(cf-ap20).  All configuration and pricing services tenants of a customer must be operated in the same data center. It is not possible to run one tenant on AWS and another on Azure, nor to switch data centers for existing tenants.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-19\nValid as Of: 2025-10-22\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 30 ---\nComponent: Variant Configuration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Pre-Production - Configurations API – Dependency Profiling Trace\nDescription: With the dependency profiling trace, it is possible to measure the runtimes of dependencies to analyze the model performance. For on-request tracing, the header parameter x-cps-trace: DEPENDENCY_PROFILING needs to be used. Dependency execution runtimes and counts are recorded and displayed in the administration UI for the configuration service in the section Configuration  Trace   Dependency Profiling Trace.  Dependency profiling is unavailable for products processed through AVC Forwarding. Only dependencies executed within the native engine of the Variant Configuration service will be profiled.  See: Development Guide for SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing, and Administration Guide for SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-19\nValid as Of: 2025-10-22\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 2541 ---\nComponent: Cloud Logging\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Updates\nDescription: We have improved Kyma and Cloud Foundry dashboards by fixing the error visualization in the 4 Golden Signal to show the correct values when filtering.  We have improved ingestion stability by fixing sporadic 502 responses from the ingest endpoint.  We've removed never-supported email destinations from the alerting plugin dropdown.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-07-25\nValid as Of: 2024-07-25\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2542 ---\nComponent: Cloud Management Tools,SAP BTP Cockpit\nEnvironment: ABAP,Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo,Other\nTitle: New Chart - Global Account Cost Summary\nDescription: In the Costs and Usage page in the SAP BTP cockpit, we've added a new Global Account - Cost Summary chart that summarizes the costs by month in your global account for the last 12 months.  You can find this chart in the Billing view under the main table when you haven't selected a service, subaccount, or directory in the main table.  See Monitoring Usage and Consumption Costs in Your Global Account.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-07-25\nValid as Of: 2024-07-25\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2543 ---\nComponent: Continuous Integration & Delivery\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Region Available\nDescription: SAP Continuous Integration and Delivery can now also be consumed in the Europe (Netherlands) region. See Regional Availability.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-07-25\nValid as Of: 2024-07-25\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2544 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Data Center Availability\nDescription: The following attributes are added to Client Information:     Europe (Netherlands) of Microsoft Azure (EU20)      Europe (Frankfurt) of Google Cloud Platform (EU30)      US East (VA) of Microsoft Azure (US21)      US Central (IA) of Google Cloud Platform (US30)     See Data Centers Supported by Joule.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-07-25\nValid as Of: 2024-07-25\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2545 ---\nComponent: Multitarget Applications for Cloud Foundry\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New dependency-specific parameter\nDescription: You can now use the new binding-name parameter in the requires section to specify the name of the binding.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-07-15\nValid as Of: 2024-07-25\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2546 ---\nComponent: SAP Audit Log\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Filter your audit log data based on categories\nDescription: With the Retrieval API, it is now possible to filter your audit log data based on categories. The predefined audit log categories available for selection include: \"audit.security-events\", \"audit.data-access\", \"audit.data-modification\", and \"audit.configuration\". For more information, see Audit Log Retrieval API Usage for Subaccounts in the Cloud Foundry Environment\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-07-19\nValid as Of: 2024-07-25\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2547 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP Best Practices\nEnvironment: ABAP,Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo,Other\nTitle: Best Practices Guide - Update\nDescription: Find recommendations about SAP Cloud Transport Management and SAP Cloud ALM in Delivering Applications, improved guidance for Configuring Backup and Naming Conventions for SAP BTP Accounts, and an example for using both, Cloud Foundry runtime and Kyma runtime in Creating a Staged Development Environment.  Stay informed with the new page What's New for SAP BTP Best Practices.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-07-24\nValid as Of: 2024-07-25\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2548 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Runtime\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Version 40.18.0\nDescription: Cloud Foundry has been updated from 40.17.0 to 40.18.0.  https://github.com/cloudfoundry/cf-deployment/releases/tag/v40.18.0  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-07-25\nValid as Of: 2024-07-25\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2549 ---\nComponent: SAP Java Buildpack\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Version 1.99.1\nDescription: SAP Java Buildpack 1 has been updated from version 1.98.1 to 1.99.1. Updated components:      Apache TomEE 7 is updated from version 7.0.9.sap-43 to 7.0.9.sap-44      SAP HANA Driver (hana.driver.2.X.X) is updated from version 2.21", " Java Buildpack\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Version 1.99.1\nDescription: SAP Java Buildpack 1 has been updated from version 1.98.1 to 1.99.1. Updated components:      Apache TomEE 7 is updated from version 7.0.9.sap-43 to 7.0.9.sap-44      SAP HANA Driver (hana.driver.2.X.X) is upda